      "after": null,
      "text_diff": "@@ -1,13 +1,14 @@\n Claude desktop app only.\n Where your allow list and deny list apply to MCP servers added in the Claude desktop app.\n-\"code\" (default): Your allow list also governs MCP servers added in the Claude desktop app, in Code tab sessions and the Artifact pane.\n-\"all\": Your allow list and your deny list also govern MCP servers added in the Claude desktop app, in every tab (including Chat and Cowork).\n+\"code\" (default): Your allow list also governs MCP servers added in the Claude desktop app, in local Code tab sessions and the Artifact pane.\n+\"all\": Same as \"code\".\n+Your allow list and deny list also govern MCP servers in the app's config file (Settings > Developer > Edit config), in every tab (including Chat and Cowork) and when the app sends them to an SSH host.\n \"off\": Your allow list doesn't govern MCP servers added in the Claude desktop app.\n Read only from managed settings.\n Any other value counts as `all`.\n Where sources are merged or mixed, `off` counts as `all`.\n Leave the key out, or set it only in the managed source that holds your list.\n-`deniedMcpServers` applies in Code tab sessions and the Artifact pane with every value, and in every tab with `all`.\n-MCP servers sent to SSH hosts are not governed by these lists in this release.\n+`deniedMcpServers` applies in local Code tab sessions and the Artifact pane with every value.\n+MCP servers that the app sends to SSH hosts are governed by these lists, and by `strictPluginOnlyCustomization` for MCP, only with `all`, and not by older versions of the app.\n The Claude Code CLI reads nothing from this key, but written alone in a higher managed source it makes that source lead, and Claude Code skips the managed sources beneath it.\n Write it only beside the list it scopes.\n",
